WEBVTT

00:02.001 --> 00:03.014
(Class 3-1)

00:03.014 --> 00:05.531
(Sports Festival)

00:05.823 --> 00:10.802
Only 19 days, 18 hours, and 23 minutes
until your last Sports Festival in middle school!

00:10.953 --> 00:12.304
Don't be so serious about it...

00:12.304 --> 00:14.289
That's how you were
for Valentine's, though.

00:14.568 --> 00:19.770
Last year, my blue team suffered
a crushing defeat in 3rd place!

00:19.770 --> 00:24.800
This year, we will win with our
unity, dedication, and hard work!

00:24.800 --> 00:28.904
I want to stand on top
of the other teachers!

00:28.904 --> 00:30.180
You're too honest!

00:30.597 --> 00:32.281
I hate this...

00:33.058 --> 00:34.017
And that's how

00:34.476 --> 00:39.398
the annual most pointless event in school
is about to start.

00:40.107 --> 00:41.483
I hate this so much.

00:42.943 --> 00:43.819
Hey.

00:45.404 --> 00:46.780
Ichikawa.

00:47.258 --> 00:49.324
Be our rider, will you?

00:51.535 --> 00:52.511
Rider?

02:23.961 --> 02:24.811
Rider?

02:26.004 --> 02:28.048
Be on top in the cavalry battle.

02:28.423 --> 02:29.716
Why me?

02:29.716 --> 02:32.694
I mean, because you're tiny?

02:32.694 --> 02:34.554
- And you've got guts...
- He's not tiny!

02:39.977 --> 02:43.163
And you've got guts, I thought,
but I'll find someone else.

02:43.163 --> 02:45.248
Oh, b-but he does have guts!

02:45.248 --> 02:46.817
It's fine, it's fine!

02:48.902 --> 02:51.154
Oh? And you said no?

02:51.446 --> 02:52.239
Yeah, well.

02:52.739 --> 02:53.949
I'm doing it.

02:54.283 --> 02:57.869
But I wish they'd let us
make a team with girls.

02:58.078 --> 02:59.590
Make them all wear swimsuits,

02:59.591 --> 03:01.431
and instead of taking headbands to win
we'll take bikinis...

03:01.431 --> 03:03.542
Is this a TV program in the Showa age?

03:04.001 --> 03:05.585
But, you know... huh?

03:06.311 --> 03:07.521
W-What?

03:07.796 --> 03:11.800
No, I just noticed
how much taller you've grown.

03:12.134 --> 03:14.303
Did your thighs also get plump?

03:14.594 --> 03:16.594
Who cares about that!

03:17.306 --> 03:20.434
You got injured in
the sports festival last year, right?

03:20.642 --> 03:21.435
Huh?

03:21.727 --> 03:25.147
You know, when you were
doing the centipede race...

03:32.529 --> 03:33.322
Ah.

03:33.780 --> 03:35.407
Sorry about back then.

03:35.741 --> 03:38.994
I said you pulled
Yamada down, and stuff...

03:39.453 --> 03:41.288
It's fine.
I don't even remember about that.

03:42.205 --> 03:44.416
Yamada told me after that.

03:45.042 --> 03:46.047
I don't think so.

03:46.047 --> 03:49.504
I think he took my fall
so that I won't get injured.

03:49.963 --> 03:54.468
Back then, I thought,
"Wow, Yamada's such a nice person..."

03:54.926 --> 03:55.761
I...

03:56.511 --> 03:57.554
Wait, he's gone!

03:59.222 --> 04:00.640
Thinking about it now,

04:01.224 --> 04:03.977
I think that was my first
real contact with Yamada.

04:05.937 --> 04:08.874
Alright, let's go!

04:08.874 --> 04:12.319
One, two, one two...

04:12.569 --> 04:14.988
Why is Anna Yamada here?

04:14.988 --> 04:18.408
All gathered up here with us rejects?

04:19.451 --> 04:22.095
Oh, right. Didn't she say she's a model?

04:22.287 --> 04:27.334
Is she trying to stand out? Standing here
with us to make herself brighter?

04:28.877 --> 04:29.961
I wanna die.

04:31.271 --> 04:32.881
- Ichikawa.
- W-Wha...

04:33.507 --> 04:36.218
Come to think of it,
in last year's sports festival...

04:37.110 --> 04:39.279
A-Are you okay?

04:40.097 --> 04:41.181
I hate this.

04:41.807 --> 04:43.016
I hate this!

04:47.771 --> 04:50.524
Ah, you've got the scar still...

04:52.734 --> 04:53.652
I'm sorry.

04:54.753 --> 04:55.695
Thank you.

05:00.826 --> 05:01.785
Adachi?

05:02.577 --> 05:04.287
Huh? What's wrong?

05:04.746 --> 05:05.664
Kanzaki.

05:06.289 --> 05:10.377
You were with Yamada and
Ichikawa on White Day, right?

05:11.795 --> 05:14.648
I told you to not tell Adachi about that!

05:14.648 --> 05:15.549
Sorry!

05:19.428 --> 05:20.887
H-Hey...

05:23.890 --> 05:26.309
Ichikawa. Be a rider.

05:26.309 --> 05:27.077
What?

05:27.853 --> 05:29.104
Let's do it man to man.

05:34.276 --> 05:35.835
Not a single reaction?!

05:35.835 --> 05:38.505
I mean, you don't have to do it
if you don't want to!

05:38.505 --> 05:39.281
I...

05:42.033 --> 05:43.869
I'll... do it if you want.

05:45.856 --> 05:47.164
Doing it because of me?

05:52.461 --> 05:54.880
This stand-off doesn't mean anything.

06:00.152 --> 06:03.388
But somehow... I don't wanna lose!

06:05.557 --> 06:06.391
I don't wanna...

06:07.350 --> 06:10.161
Dammit! My pace was all wrong!

06:15.317 --> 06:19.321
They say you're not gonna get taller
if you get too built when you're young...

06:19.654 --> 06:21.573
I guess I'll stop here for now.

06:22.157 --> 06:23.867
No, that's not right.

06:24.159 --> 06:27.954
A lot of athletes trained their bodies
since they were little.

06:28.346 --> 06:29.873
T-That's...

06:30.373 --> 06:31.891
You should look it up.

06:32.125 --> 06:35.312
No way. My algorithm would think
I like buffing up.

06:35.670 --> 06:38.356
Go! I shouldn't talk to myself outside.

06:39.633 --> 06:41.426
Come on, there's a dog here, too...

06:55.023 --> 06:57.023
- Whaddaya want?
- Don't be so cold!

06:58.735 --> 07:01.212
I was talking with Wantaro.

07:01.530 --> 07:02.964
You should talk with words.

07:02.964 --> 07:04.741
Dogs don't understand words.

07:05.158 --> 07:06.743
They don't understand either way.

07:07.452 --> 07:10.080
Are you perhaps training
for the sports festival?

07:11.164 --> 07:12.493
Not that.

07:12.747 --> 07:16.795
If I'm too weak, it'll give me trouble
when the world gets infested by zombies.

07:18.647 --> 07:20.882
The world can suddenly just change
in the blink of an eye, you know.

07:21.299 --> 07:23.593
When that happens,
you can only rely on yourself.

07:23.927 --> 07:25.220
That's true.

07:25.804 --> 07:27.347
Alright! Then...

07:27.722 --> 07:28.682
Let's train together!

07:37.983 --> 07:39.609
How far are you taking me?

07:44.531 --> 07:46.491
Alright! Goal!

07:49.494 --> 07:52.263
Yamada's really
way more athletic than I am...

07:52.263 --> 07:53.540
Oh, right!

07:54.416 --> 07:58.003
I have a lot of tools in my house,
wanna do it with them?

07:59.004 --> 07:59.921
Tools?

08:00.672 --> 08:01.923
Do it?

08:03.174 --> 08:05.844
My mom is out gathering in Toyosu today.

08:06.177 --> 08:09.055
This is not a healthy direction...

08:09.347 --> 08:12.017
Ta-da! This mysterious tool!

08:12.284 --> 08:13.785
What is this, now?

08:13.785 --> 08:15.495
An ab roller, right?

08:15.770 --> 08:17.897
This is pretty effective.

08:18.481 --> 08:19.858
Of course.

08:20.150 --> 08:22.277
Yamada's not that unhealthy.

08:23.320 --> 08:26.323
This... might be unhealthy, though?!

08:27.157 --> 08:29.701
S-So you work out at home, huh?

08:30.118 --> 08:32.010
Sorry if this is rude,
but that doesn't seem right.

08:32.162 --> 08:35.190
There are no girls who aren't on a diet...

08:37.125 --> 08:38.934
Get him to move!

08:38.934 --> 08:41.020
Hurry!

08:43.089 --> 08:44.633
Move. Move!

08:45.175 --> 08:47.110
Dogs are heavier than they look...

08:52.741 --> 08:53.767
Which one of you?

08:54.058 --> 08:55.310
Huh? Which one of us what?

08:57.729 --> 08:59.397
Sixteen...

08:59.898 --> 09:01.775
Seventeen...

09:02.108 --> 09:03.777
Eighteen...

09:05.904 --> 09:07.614
This is harder than it looks.

09:07.614 --> 09:09.007
Oop!

09:09.324 --> 09:11.451
My dad's dumbbell. Try lifting it.

09:12.035 --> 09:15.538
There's no way I'd be able
to lift something you can't.

09:15.872 --> 09:18.875
Huh? But you're doing a man-to-man thing.

09:19.668 --> 09:21.503
Sorry if this is rude,
but that doesn't seem right.

09:23.546 --> 09:26.174
That's the first one I've heard
"man-to-man" in real life.

09:26.466 --> 09:27.467
Why did you accept?

09:29.177 --> 09:30.261
Because Adachi...

09:31.012 --> 09:32.055
...is my friend.

09:33.932 --> 09:35.517
You're serious about this, huh?

09:36.226 --> 09:36.935
Yeah.

09:38.520 --> 09:41.314
Adachi likes Yamada.

09:42.315 --> 09:43.608
Let's do it man to man.

09:44.359 --> 09:47.153
Maybe... he also knows
about me and Yamada...

09:50.532 --> 09:52.383
K-Kyotaro,

09:52.867 --> 09:56.413
do you prefer your eggs salty or sweet?

09:56.955 --> 09:58.456
But I still don't want to lose!

09:59.541 --> 10:01.643
Because I'm the one who loves Yamada...

10:02.585 --> 10:05.213
I-I prefer it sweet...

10:07.340 --> 10:09.676
...so much more!

10:11.402 --> 10:13.096
A-Ah!

10:13.096 --> 10:14.180
Watch out!

10:18.643 --> 10:20.770
You like it sweet that much?

10:21.312 --> 10:22.188
Yeah.

10:23.022 --> 10:23.982
Then...

10:24.441 --> 10:26.985
You don't have to bring lunch
on the festival day.

10:28.027 --> 10:29.446
I'm also going to do my best!

10:29.921 --> 10:31.114
In what?

10:31.990 --> 10:33.450
(Class 3-1)

10:37.162 --> 10:38.204
Peace!

10:39.581 --> 10:44.502
Because we're 3rd-years now,
we get to do this shamelessly!

10:47.464 --> 10:48.474
Alright!

10:48.475 --> 10:49.883
(Original)
All done!

10:50.341 --> 10:52.443
What's that? Your you-know-what's name?

10:52.443 --> 10:53.862
It's from Moko Tanmen Ramen's packaging.

10:54.012 --> 10:55.096
Moko?

10:55.597 --> 10:59.100
And thus came the day
of the sports festival.

11:02.103 --> 11:03.229
- Wha...
- Stay still.

11:06.649 --> 11:08.902
That's... not permanent, right?

11:17.952 --> 11:19.871
Never take that off, okay?

11:25.668 --> 11:27.420
The forecast said it'll
start to rain at noon.

11:27.962 --> 11:32.759
I mean, I don't care if I get rained on.
In fact, I'd love that.

11:33.343 --> 11:34.886
Time for the athlete's oath.

11:38.097 --> 11:41.267
Adachi practiced a lot yesterday.

11:42.661 --> 11:44.661
He's... serious.

11:45.480 --> 11:46.731
Teachers!

11:47.190 --> 11:50.610
We're loaded... with sportsmanship!

11:51.069 --> 11:53.446
And we will fight fair and square!

11:53.780 --> 11:55.142
Until we come... to win!

11:59.869 --> 12:02.138
Wow! He did it!

12:02.138 --> 12:04.082
He went with the harder one!

12:04.249 --> 12:07.310
I thought he was actually serious!

12:07.310 --> 12:10.004
I'll never lose to a guy like him!

12:12.407 --> 12:15.635
(Anna Yamada) (Look at me)
Look. I made support fans.

12:15.969 --> 12:17.470
She shouldn't look at you.

12:17.679 --> 12:19.222
Ah. Really?

12:19.514 --> 12:22.392
Hanzawa, you're really just
a more crafty Yamada, huh?

12:26.104 --> 12:28.857
Borrowing contest, borrowing contest...

12:32.861 --> 12:34.861
Wow! Whoooa!

12:34.861 --> 12:35.630
What?

12:35.630 --> 12:38.132
Wow! It says "couple"!

12:38.132 --> 12:40.618
"Mutual feelings OK", it says!

12:41.786 --> 12:43.763
She clearly made it herself...

12:44.122 --> 12:46.557
Gotta borrow a couple!
Give me a hot couple!

12:48.710 --> 12:50.587
- A. Yamada.
- I don't...

12:50.879 --> 12:52.855
(Look at me)
But it says to look at you.

12:53.606 --> 12:55.258
Then, you know any other couples?

13:00.930 --> 13:02.807
U-Um...

13:08.229 --> 13:09.981
First place!

13:09.981 --> 13:11.858
Yuki, put me down...

13:12.734 --> 13:13.943
Je t'aime...

13:14.360 --> 13:15.737
It's invalid, so you're disqualified.

13:20.658 --> 13:23.870
Didn't I tell you that
I really want us to win?

13:24.662 --> 13:26.581
So it really was a trap.

13:27.790 --> 13:28.875
Warming up?

13:32.545 --> 13:33.671
Anna!

13:33.671 --> 13:35.648
Come on, Yamada!

13:35.648 --> 13:37.525
Don't play around!

13:38.968 --> 13:40.595
Yamadaaaa?!

13:41.471 --> 13:44.824
Wait, this guy! He just never changes!

13:45.308 --> 13:47.435
But, fine then!

13:55.652 --> 13:57.528
This is what happened last time, too.

13:57.946 --> 14:00.073
You've also blocked me before, Ichikawa.

14:13.419 --> 14:15.171
It started raining.

14:15.421 --> 14:19.175
We'll discuss how to go about
the rest of the matches.

14:19.676 --> 14:22.261
Please wait for a little while.

14:22.553 --> 14:26.808
This might cancel the cavalry battle
and allow us to eat lunch early, Yamada.

14:32.397 --> 14:34.070
We'll have to cancel the rest...

14:34.071 --> 14:36.067
No, it's just a light drizzle.

14:37.568 --> 14:39.320
This much is fine!

14:39.988 --> 14:41.589
Oh? Adachi?

14:41.589 --> 14:44.300
Only boys are playing,
so getting wet is not a problem.

14:44.300 --> 14:45.868
That's not the problem here...

14:46.035 --> 14:46.953
Let's do it.

14:48.705 --> 14:50.373
It'll finish in no time.

14:51.082 --> 14:53.626
The one who will put an end
to this dreadful event...

14:55.336 --> 14:56.254
...is me.

15:02.760 --> 15:04.470
Once it starts, go straight ahead!

15:05.596 --> 15:06.514
Just do it!

15:07.181 --> 15:08.558
Fine.

15:08.891 --> 15:10.785
The rain has gotten stronger.

15:10.785 --> 15:12.895
Come on, let's just get inside.

15:13.896 --> 15:15.023
Ichikawa...

15:19.027 --> 15:20.737
This is for Adachi's sake.

15:21.487 --> 15:22.447
Is it really?

15:23.281 --> 15:27.035
Or is it for that awful thing I hate
called friendship?

15:28.077 --> 15:31.205
No! It's not that noble of a cause!

15:31.956 --> 15:33.583
I just...

15:34.667 --> 15:35.793
I just...

15:35.793 --> 15:39.130
I love Anna Yamada!

15:41.758 --> 15:43.760
I mean... I also...

15:43.760 --> 15:44.844
But!

15:45.428 --> 15:47.972
I think you're a good guy, Ichikawa!

15:48.890 --> 15:50.767
So... so!

15:51.517 --> 15:52.827
Don't give me that crap!

15:53.644 --> 15:57.065
You don't know anything about me.
Don't say that I'm a good guy!

15:57.940 --> 16:02.612
You don't know anything about Yamada!
Don't just say that you love her!

16:03.029 --> 16:04.739
That friendship chocolate you got...

16:05.156 --> 16:09.911
You thought that thing was fate!
So don't say that you like Yamada!

16:09.911 --> 16:12.872
- I know that already!
- No, you don't!

16:13.414 --> 16:14.540
Yamada is...

16:14.874 --> 16:17.168
...more mature than guys like us!

16:17.168 --> 16:19.308
She runs to chase her dream!

16:19.309 --> 16:21.881
She works harder than anyone else!
She's an amazing person!

16:22.215 --> 16:25.109
Just because she's cute,
or that she's stylish...

16:25.109 --> 16:27.470
You shouldn't like her
just because of that!

16:27.470 --> 16:29.722
Love is... Love is...

16:30.056 --> 16:31.808
Love is not something like that!

16:32.767 --> 16:34.393
I know that.

16:35.144 --> 16:38.481
And I've... probably lost.

16:39.248 --> 16:40.375
So...

16:40.858 --> 16:44.195
Because I've lost,
just let me lose pathetically.

16:47.365 --> 16:48.741
I can't acknowledge that.

16:49.617 --> 16:51.077
Don't give me that crap!

16:51.077 --> 16:52.386
- Don't give me that!
- Huh?!

16:52.386 --> 16:54.163
That's how you feel, right?!

16:54.789 --> 16:58.167
You're serious about it, right?!
Then don't just accept it!

16:58.459 --> 17:00.169
Say that you're serious!

17:00.169 --> 17:02.380
And what'll happen if I do say it?!

17:02.380 --> 17:04.257
Nothing will!

17:04.257 --> 17:05.191
Yeah!

17:05.191 --> 17:06.384
I'm serious!

17:07.009 --> 17:10.512
I do seriously love Yamada!

17:12.348 --> 17:15.143
- It's so cold.
- Let's get below the tent.

17:15.685 --> 17:19.063
I couldn't hear them,
but seems like they were talking.

17:21.732 --> 17:23.233
Let's keep watching for a bit.

17:24.443 --> 17:26.362
What are you telling me to do, huh?!

17:26.695 --> 17:27.922
Who the hell knows!

17:27.922 --> 17:31.242
You're the one who said we'll go
man-to-man! So take this seriously!

17:31.242 --> 17:32.760
Dammit...

17:33.244 --> 17:36.747
I didn't know you were
this kind of guy, Ichikawa...

17:40.960 --> 17:45.631
I was just about to start hating Yamada!

17:46.924 --> 17:48.426
("I...")

17:51.429 --> 17:53.429
("...Don't Want to Lose")

17:53.429 --> 17:56.851
(Kyo)

17:56.851 --> 17:58.244
Kyo!

18:09.614 --> 18:12.867
("I Don't Want to Lose")

18:26.964 --> 18:28.674
Dammit...

18:32.094 --> 18:33.095
I'm glad...

18:34.013 --> 18:35.806
...that it's raining.

18:36.390 --> 18:38.726
(Nurse's Office)

18:40.102 --> 18:41.395
Ichikawa.

18:41.395 --> 18:43.105
Now, now...

18:43.814 --> 18:45.691
Go home already, mom.

18:45.983 --> 18:48.069
Don't underestimate me!
I've got a nursing license!

18:51.197 --> 18:52.323
Bye, now.

19:07.588 --> 19:08.673
What?

19:11.217 --> 19:12.677
It's soaking wet.

19:17.932 --> 19:19.267
She's kinda cute.

19:20.393 --> 19:22.937
Are you maybe... Ichikawa's sister?!

19:25.690 --> 19:26.565
Brat.

19:26.565 --> 19:27.917
Ack!

19:30.569 --> 19:31.445
I lost.

19:34.740 --> 19:37.618
My mom often told me...

19:38.327 --> 19:40.538
...that you shouldn't forget
the anger that you feel.

19:40.871 --> 19:44.333
That's the most important thing that
can drive you forward.

19:45.876 --> 19:46.961
Anger...

19:48.004 --> 19:51.257
I was trying so hard to
suppress that emotion back then.

19:52.568 --> 19:54.093
I'll put this here.

19:54.844 --> 19:55.636
Is that...

19:56.012 --> 19:57.263
Yeah, your lunch box.

19:57.972 --> 19:59.557
I-It's huge.

19:59.890 --> 20:01.976
This is the best one I made.

20:02.519 --> 20:03.311
O-Okay.

20:03.602 --> 20:05.396
Also, I've got fried chicken.

20:06.439 --> 20:08.290
- Those are rice balls.
- The filling, I mean.

20:08.290 --> 20:09.442
All of them?

20:10.318 --> 20:11.777
Wanna eat some omelet?

20:14.071 --> 20:15.114
Ah, crap!

20:15.281 --> 20:18.993
I'm the type to not mince my words.
If it's bad, I'll say it straight out...

20:21.037 --> 20:21.662
It's good.

20:23.180 --> 20:24.248
Thank you.

20:24.498 --> 20:26.475
No, it's not just me
trying to flatter you.

20:26.751 --> 20:29.003
It's not too sweet, tastes great,
and cooked well...

20:38.763 --> 20:40.448
N-No!

20:40.448 --> 20:43.225
It's not that I wanted a bite,
I was just looking at you and...

20:43.768 --> 20:45.853
- It's good.
- Eat some too, Yamada.

20:46.354 --> 20:48.354
It's all for you, Kyotaro.

20:48.564 --> 20:51.067
You thought I eat like a wrestler?

20:51.400 --> 20:53.694
Then, I'll also bring mine here.

20:53.694 --> 20:56.030
N-No, it's fine!
People will start to think things.

21:00.951 --> 21:02.328
- Hey.
- Hm?

21:03.746 --> 21:04.789
You're so...

21:05.915 --> 21:06.957
...cool, today!
